>> name: 炒飯
>> description: A quick and satisfying classic fried rice. Best made with day-old rice.
>> servings: 2
>> tags: rice, quick, chinese

Cook @rice{200%g} in a rice cooker, then spread on a tray to cool for at least 30 minutes.
Beat @eggs{2} with a pinch of @salt{} in a small bowl.
Heat @cooking oil{1%tbsp} in a #wok{} over high heat until smoking.
Pour in the egg mixture, scramble briefly until just set, then push to the side.
Add the cooled rice, breaking up any clumps, and stir-fry for ~{2%min}.
Drizzle @soy sauce{1%tbsp} and @sesame oil{1%tsp} around the edge of the wok.
Toss everything together for ~{1%min}, season with @salt{to taste}, and serve.
